From: erenmakal <erenmakal@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 05:20:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Avoid blocking offline player name lookup on Folia

OfflinePlayerStub#setName receives a name that Essentials already resolved
from its own user data or caller context. Prefer that supplied value instead
of calling Bukkit OfflinePlayer#getName first.

On Canvas/Folia, CraftOfflinePlayer#getName may synchronously read the
vanilla playerdata NBT file. When balance providers iterate many offline
users from the global region, that disk I/O can stall the global tick long
enough to trip the Folia watchdog.

Keep the Bukkit lookup only as a fallback when no name was supplied so
legacy behaviour is preserved for callers that genuinely do not know it.

diff --git a/providers/1_12Provider/src/main/java/com/earth2me/essentials/OfflinePlayerStub.java b/providers/1_12Provider/src/main/java/com/earth2me/essentials/OfflinePlayerStub.java
--- a/providers/1_12Provider/src/main/java/com/earth2me/essentials/OfflinePlayerStub.java
+++ b/providers/1_12Provider/src/main/java/com/earth2me/essentials/OfflinePlayerStub.java
@@ -1341,9 +1341,9 @@ public class OfflinePlayerStub implements Player {
     }
 
     public void setName(final String name) {
-        this.name = base.getName();
+        this.name = name;
         if (this.name == null) {
-            this.name = name;
+            this.name = base.getName();
         }
     }
 
